From: Christopher Owen <3221756+christopherowen@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sun, 4 Oct 2026 14:27:23 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] Route DeepSeek V4.1 with TileKernels' TileLang top-k gate

The TileLang kernel family routed the target's MoE layers through vLLM's
Triton dsv4_topk and the drafter's through a CUDA op. Both now use
TileKernels' moe_topk_gate_forward, DeepSeek's TileLang router. It
implements the V4.1 reference: sqrt(softplus) scores, the top-k of score
plus the correction bias (the vision bias for image tokens) with the lowest
expert first on ties, and the chosen scores normalized by their sum plus
1e-20 and scaled. Its scores are bit-identical to torch's sqrt(softplus).
It refuses non-finite logits.

The image-token mask is computed once per step and shared by every layer.
DeepseekV4MoE takes the router class from the kernel family. B12X keeps
vLLM's router, and MegaMoE, which routes in its own kernel, refuses one.
